# GroundWork — environment configuration
# Copy to .env.local for local development (.env.local is gitignored).
# Full walkthrough: docs/SETUP.md

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# CONTEXT_MODE — the fidelity switch
#   mock      (default) Mode 1 — SQLite seed data. Boots with no AWS.
#   ontology            Mode 2 — answers driven by the OWL packs in packs/.
#                                Still no AWS. Transitive reasoning + governed metrics.
#   coa                 Mode 3 — resolved over a live Context Ontology Accelerator
#                                you deploy in your own AWS account.
CONTEXT_MODE=mock

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Mode 3 (CONTEXT_MODE=coa) — YOUR deployed COA endpoint. See docs/SETUP.md and
# docs/MODE3_COA.md for how to deploy COA and obtain each value below.
#
# Easiest path once these are set: `npm run demo:coa` mints a fresh COA_TOKEN
# from Cognito (tokens expire ~1h) and launches with the stale token unset.

# The invoke URL of your COA API (API Gateway stage URL).
# COA_BASE_URL=https://<your-api-id>.execute-api.<region>.amazonaws.com/prod

# Query transport (Mode 3). Default "rest" uses COA_BASE_URL above — simple and
# portable, but API Gateway caps a response at ~29s, so a long graph synthesis
# can 504. Set "agentcore" to send the `query` call over COA's AgentCore Runtime
# SSE endpoint instead (no 29s cap; serve allows ~170s). Requires
# COA_SERVE_RUNTIME_ARN. Fast tools (metrics/schema/traverse) always use REST,
# and any AgentCore failure falls back to REST automatically.
# COA_TRANSPORT=rest
# The serve runtime ARN — on a COA deployment it's in SSM at
# /<your-coa-prefix>/serve/runtime-arn (e.g. /my-coa-dev/serve/runtime-arn).
# COA_SERVE_RUNTIME_ARN=arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:<region>:<account>:runtime/<id>

# Cognito app client id + user credentials the mint script uses. Keep the
# password in .env.local only — never commit it.
# COA_CLIENT_ID=<your-cognito-app-client-id>
# COA_USER=you@example.com
# COA_PASS=<your-cognito-user-password>

# COA_TOKEN is auto-minted by scripts/demo-coa.sh — leave it unset.
# COA_TOKEN=

# IMPORTANT: COA's data-plane endpoints (kb/search, graph/traverse, query)
# resolve a namespace by its UUID, NOT its friendly name. Using the name
# (e.g. "otsec") returns 0 chunks / 0 nodes SILENTLY. Use the UUID from
# `GET /namespaces` on your deployment (one per vertical you install a pack into).
# The variable is COA_NAMESPACE_<VERTICAL_ID_UPPERCASE>; a vertical whose
# variable is set counts as Live-COA-configured (/api/mode → coaVerticals), and
# the Sources view (/api/sources) needs the UUID. The value never reaches the
# browser. Unset → falls back to the pack directory name.
# COA_NAMESPACE_OTSEC=<your-otsec-namespace-uuid>
# COA_NAMESPACE_PRODQUALITY=<your-prodquality-namespace-uuid>
# COA_NAMESPACE_ENERGY=<your-energy-namespace-uuid>
# COA_NAMESPACE_MANUFACTURING=<your-manufacturing-namespace-uuid>
# COA_NAMESPACE_CYBER=<your-cyber-namespace-uuid>

# Mode 3 tuning (optional)
# COA_VECTOR_TIMEOUT_MS=25000         # vector search budget per query
# COA_TRAVERSE_TIMEOUT_MS=2500        # graph traverse budget
# COA_DISABLE_CACHE=1                 # skip the hero-answer cache, force live COA

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AWS — used by real Bedrock generation and Titan embeddings, and by Mode 3.
# The demo runs with NO AWS by default; these only matter when you enable the
# backends below or use Mode 3.
AWS_REGION=us-west-2
AWS_PROFILE=default                  # a named CLI profile with access to your account
# S3_BUCKET=<your-data-bucket>

# Turn on REAL AWS (the two flips). Leave unset for the laptop demo.
# GENERATION_BACKEND=bedrock         # graph answers synthesized by a real Bedrock model
# EMBEDDINGS_BACKEND=titan           # vector retrieval uses real Titan embeddings
DEFAULT_MODEL_ID=nova-pro            # registry id; see src/lib/models.ts
# TITAN_EMBED_MODEL_ID=amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0   # default; 1024-dim
# Bedrock entity extraction for /api/extract (optional; regex extraction otherwise)
# BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=<bedrock-model-or-inference-profile-id>

# Local SQLite path (default <cwd>/groundwork.db; containers use /tmp/groundwork.db)
# DB_PATH=/tmp/groundwork.db

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Access gate — FAILS CLOSED. The server binds 127.0.0.1, and every page and API
# route except /api/health answers 503 "setup required" until ONE of these is set:
#
#   a) the login gate: all three of DEMO_USER, DEMO_PASS and AUTH_SECRET.
#      Required for any shared or hosted deployment (see docs/DEPLOY_PUBLIC.md).
#      Generate AUTH_SECRET with: openssl rand -base64 32
DEMO_USER=
DEMO_PASS=
AUTH_SECRET=
#
#   b) local-only bypass (no login). Only the exact value "true" is honored.
#      Use it on your own machine on 127.0.0.1; NEVER on a shared deployment.
# AUTH_LOCAL_BYPASS=true

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Amazon Quick MCP proxy (tools/quick-mcp-proxy) — optional.
# The proxy is a separate process and reads these from ITS environment (export
# them, or `node --env-file=<file>`); the Next.js app ignores them. Full guide:
# docs/QUICK_MCP_INTEGRATION.md. It also uses COA_BASE_URL / COA_CLIENT_ID /
# COA_USER / COA_PASS / COA_TOKEN / COA_TRANSPORT / COA_SERVE_RUNTIME_ARN /
# COA_NAMESPACE_* / AWS_REGION from the Mode 3 section above.
#
# Network — loopback by default. A non-loopback bind requires QUICK_OAUTH_ISSUER.
# BIND_HOST=127.0.0.1
# PORT=8787
# MCP_PATH=/mcp
#
# Inbound auth for Quick's "Service authentication" (OAuth client_credentials).
# QUICK_OAUTH_ISSUER=https://cognito-idp.<region>.amazonaws.com/<user-pool-id>
# QUICK_OAUTH_CLIENT_IDS=<quick-app-client-id>
# QUICK_OAUTH_AUDIENCE=<expected-aud-if-your-idp-sets-one>
# QUICK_OAUTH_REQUIRED_SCOPE=<resource-server-id>/query
# QUICK_OAUTH_JWKS_URL=<override; default <issuer>/.well-known/jwks.json>
#
# LOCAL TESTING ONLY (honored on a loopback bind only): a random bearer value
# for curl / `npm run smoke`, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`. Never deploy it.
# QUICK_INBOUND_TOKENS=<random-local-test-token>
#
# COA behavior for the proxy.
# COA_DEFAULT_NAMESPACE=<your-namespace-uuid>
# COA_CACHE_DIR=<abs-path-to>/src/data/coa-cache
# COA_QUERY_TIMEOUT_MS=240000
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NVD API Key (optional — increases rate limit from 5 to 50 req/30s)
# Get a free key: https://nvd.nist.gov/developers/request-an-api-key
# NVD_API_KEY=<your-key>
